# Architecture Plan

## Proposed module structure

- `Cargo.toml`: Leptos full-stack app with Axum SSR, hydration, router, `sqlx`, `dotenvy`, `tracing`, and Docker-friendly build settings.
- `src/lib.rs`: shared app entry, Leptos shell, route wiring, server function registration, and shared types exported to client/server builds.
- `src/main.rs`: SSR server bootstrap, env loading, tracing setup, socket binding, SQLite pool creation, migration execution, and Axum app startup.
- `src/app.rs`: top-level `App` component and route-to-filter mapping for `/`, `/active`, `/completed`.
- `src/domain/todo.rs`: `Todo`, `TodoFilter`, and small request/response DTOs shared by server functions and UI.
- `src/server/mod.rs`: server-only wiring and shared error/result helpers.
- `src/server/todos.rs`: all `#[server]` todo CRUD/query functions, grouped behind one module so UI code stays thin.
- `src/db/mod.rs`: pool type alias, connection helpers, and migration runner.
- `src/components/`
  - `todo_input.rs`
  - `todo_list.rs`
  - `todo_item.rs`
  - `todo_footer.rs`
- `migrations/`: SQLx migrations, starting with the `todos` table and index.
- `style/` or `assets/`: vendored TodoMVC CSS assets bundled by `cargo-leptos`.
- `Dockerfile`: multi-stage build using `cargo leptos build --release`.

## Shared types and boundaries

- Keep `Todo` and `TodoFilter` in a shared domain module compiled for both `ssr` and `hydrate`.
- Keep database pool and SQLx details server-only; client code should only interact through `#[server]` functions.
- Prefer server functions to return domain types instead of raw SQL rows so later UI issues only depend on stable Rust structs.
- Use route path as the single source of truth for filter state; components receive the filter or derived counts rather than owning separate filter state.

## Issue dependency plan

- Foundation:
  - Issue 1 creates the Leptos/Axum skeleton.
  - Issue 2 adds env/loading/logging on top of the skeleton.
  - Issue 3 adds SQLite pool + migration bootstrapping after env config exists.
  - Issue 4 adds the first migration after SQLx is wired.
  - Issue 5 adds TodoMVC assets after the app shell exists.
- Shared model and API:
  - Issue 6 defines `Todo` and `TodoFilter` after schema is known.
  - Issues 7-10 build the server API in one layer over the shared types and DB pool.
- UI shell and components:
  - Issue 11 establishes router + shell after CSS assets and filter type exist.
  - Issue 12 depends on add flow from Issue 8 plus shell from Issue 11.
  - Issue 13 depends on query/toggle/delete flows from Issues 7, 9, and 10.
  - Issue 14 extends `TodoItem` editing on top of Issue 13.
  - Issue 15 depends on list data/counts and routing from Issues 7, 10, 11, and 13.
  - Issue 16 depends on list/footer behavior being in place.
- Delivery:
  - Issue 17 depends on a complete buildable app and finalized env/build conventions.
  - Issue 18 depends on the runnable app and Docker path.
  - Issue 19 is a final spec pass after all behavior is implemented.

## Key design decisions

- Use a single SQLite pool created once at startup and injected into Leptos server context for every server function.
- Run migrations automatically on boot so local dev, Docker, and acceptance testing behave the same way.
- Store todos with integer IDs, trimmed titles, boolean completion, and `created_at` ordering exactly as the issue scopes describe.
- Keep mutations spec-driven:
  - empty create is rejected
  - empty edit deletes the item
  - `clear_completed` and `toggle_all` live server-side to preserve reload persistence
- Minimize client-only state:
  - editing text for one row
  - pending submission/mutation state
  - route-derived filter
- Prefer a small number of stable files and modules now so later issue sessions can add behavior incrementally without restructuring.
